<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Marcelly</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1917</span><span class="sg-chain-h">first recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Madelon (I'll Be True to the Whole Regiment), sung by Arthur Fields</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1918</span><span class="sg-chain-h">English version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Amparito Farrar</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1918</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Victor Military Band with Marcel Journet</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1919</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">La Madelon de la Victoire (Lucien Boyer)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1919</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sequel</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Voyage au bout de la nuit (Louis-Ferdinand Céline)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1932</span><span class="sg-chain-h">referred to in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Madelon's Daughter, film</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1937</span><span class="sg-chain-h">referred to in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Victoire, la fille de Madelon</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1939</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sequel</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">La Madelon, film (Jean Boyer)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1955</span><span class="sg-chain-h">film based on the song</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">El Último Cuplé, film (Juan de Orduña), sung by Sara Montiel</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1957</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Qu'est devenue la Madelon ? (Charles Trenet)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1960</span><span class="sg-chain-h">answer song</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Majorette (Bénabar)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">referred to in</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec"><h2>People, places and events</h2><div class="tih-tags"><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Louis Bousquet</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Camille Robert</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Charles-Joseph Pasquier (Bach)</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Sioul</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Marcelly</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Marcel Journet</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Lucien Boyer</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Clotilde Bizolon</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Marlene Dietrich</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Line Renaud</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Jean Boyer</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Sara Montiel</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Charles Trenet</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Louis-Ferdinand Céline</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">François Genton</span><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Fontenay-sous-Bois</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Étival-Clairefontaine</span><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></div></section>
